        "username": "Silverleaf",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/silverleaf/{size}/2332_2.png",
        "created_at": "2014-11-05T19:27:28.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Reckless\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/reckless/48/2467_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Reckless:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Under3 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Just a minor point, but Tempest isn't ever referred to as \"he\" in any of the background stuff.</blockquote></div>\nWhile I appreciate and emphatically approve of taking note of such things I do want to bring up that \"he\" is gender inclusive in English. \n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>\"We're not sure, so we'll assume male\" doesn't sound terribly inclusive to me.</p>",
